WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.689
Let's now talk about the Trump approval rating
on coronavirus.

00:00:05.689 --> 00:00:08.660
Hint it has absolutely imploded.

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:10.270
Now you might remember a few weeks ago.

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:13.150
Now, I guess really like three, three and
a half weeks ago.

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:17.460
Earlier in the Corona virus pandemic, we saw
that Donald Trump was sporting a pretty healthy

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:21.550
approval rating when it came to his handling
of the virus.

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:22.770
And we were wondering why.

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:28.080
And most likely it was a few things that were
sort of bullying for lack of a better term.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:31.670
Donald Trump's approval rating in general
and on the virus.

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:37.980
Number one, there was this sort of rally around
the president factor, which is often in play

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:44.170
early in a crisis where you have more people
than agree with the president politically,

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:49.500
say, I support the president and they're doing
a good job, at least so far.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:55.180
You also three and a half weeks ago had a
whole bunch of U.S. states that didn't have

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:56.180
many cases.

00:00:56.180 --> 00:01:01.960
So there were many more people in the country
that could feel rightly or wrongly like it

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:05.299
was under control because their state didn't
have many cases.

00:01:05.299 --> 00:01:09.149
Now, of course, it is a virus, meaning it
spreads virally.

00:01:09.149 --> 00:01:13.020
We now have 13 states with more than 5000
cases.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:18.299
We have 30 states with more than a thousand
cases and every single state.

00:01:18.299 --> 00:01:21.679
Other than Wyoming has had deaths.

00:01:21.679 --> 00:01:29.579
So both the reality of rally around the president
and the reality of my state is doing fine.

00:01:29.579 --> 00:01:31.179
Both of those things have changed.

00:01:31.179 --> 00:01:32.509
They've faded.

00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:35.799
And the disapproval now of Trump on the virus
is up 9 points.

00:01:35.799 --> 00:01:39.149
It was 43 percent disapproval in mid-March.

00:01:39.149 --> 00:01:41.350
It is up to 52 percent disapproval.

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:44.350
That's a climb of more than 20 percent.

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:47.920
And if things keep going the way they're going,
both in terms of the numbers and in terms

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:52.799
of Trump's unhinged response, I would expect
that disapproval on Trump's handling of the

00:01:52.799 --> 00:01:54.810
virus is going to keep going up.

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:59.770
The rally around the flag, rally around the
leader stuff is very common, but it doesn't

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:00.770
last forever.

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:03.139
And we have had one of the worst responses
total.

00:02:03.139 --> 00:02:07.429
We are testing per capita 30 nine in the world.

00:02:07.429 --> 00:02:11.030
Trump regularly claims we are doing the most
tests per capita.

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:14.540
We're not really sure he understands what
per capita means, but he claims that we're

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:16.519
doing the most tests per capita.

00:02:16.519 --> 00:02:20.129
Trump insults reporters at press conferences
who ask real questions.

00:02:20.129 --> 00:02:21.819
Trump attacks media outlets.

00:02:21.819 --> 00:02:27.189
Trump recommends dangerous behavior, suggests
medications during press conferences, brags

00:02:27.189 --> 00:02:29.910
about dating models during his press briefings.

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:35.879
And every day we are continuing to see more
and more states have these bigger and bigger

00:02:35.879 --> 00:02:37.659
numbers of cases.

00:02:37.659 --> 00:02:40.079
Eventually, it was bound to affect his approval.

00:02:40.079 --> 00:02:42.260
Now, a few things to keep in mind.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:46.580
Number one, this kind of piggybacks on our
earlier story about the World Mental Health

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:49.319
Coalition demanding Trump be removed.

00:02:49.319 --> 00:02:54.640
Number one, Trump's approval on Corona virus
may keep going down if his handling of the

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:56.340
virus remains poor.

00:02:56.340 --> 00:03:04.069
But the power of cults is very strong and
Trump has a powerful cult around him that

00:03:04.069 --> 00:03:05.700
is going to support him no matter what.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:07.890
We're going to get to that a little bit later
with some examples.

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:14.209
But just like Jim Jones got his followers
to drink cyanide laced Kool-Aid.

00:03:14.209 --> 00:03:18.900
Trump's followers are going to keep insisting
that Trump is handling this well, just like

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:22.480
Trump says he's doing during his own press
briefings.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:23.480
So we can.

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:28.760
Only expect his approval to fall a little
bit more because of that cultish support around

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:29.760
him.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:35.219
Number two, there will be no consequences
to Donald Trump's mishandling of this crisis

00:03:35.219 --> 00:03:38.319
unless we remove him in November, which means
voting.

00:03:38.319 --> 00:03:39.739
He's not going to be impeached.

00:03:39.739 --> 00:03:41.890
He's not going to be removed by the 25th Amendment.

00:03:41.890 --> 00:03:42.909
None of it.

00:03:42.909 --> 00:03:47.480
So is it good that Trump's approval on Corona
virus is coming down instead of going up?

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:48.790
Yeah, of course it's good.

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:54.650
It means some of the people in this country
are at least tangentially tied to reality.

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:59.689
But Trump's response to the virus has been
diabolical and depraved.

00:03:59.689 --> 00:04:07.030
And to see disapproval after two months at
only 52 percent is incredibly disturbing.

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:10.670
And so we just need to be realistic in our
expectations.

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:11.900
Death toll goes up.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:13.969
They claim the death toll is an accurate.

00:04:13.969 --> 00:04:16.579
We started seeing that last week.

00:04:16.579 --> 00:04:18.190
Cases spike wildly.

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:23.570
They claim it's only because our testing is
so good and so widespread.

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:28.420
So we've got to remember, they will always
talk their way out of any piece of data that

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:29.750
we can present.

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:35.260
And we can only expect the approval to fall
so much because of the cult of personality

00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:36.560
around Donald Trump.

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:37.860
And a little bit later in the show.

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:42.630
I will have some stunning, stunning video
